{"metadata":{"title":"Transactions and Services","modules":[{"name":"LoomCore"}],"roleHeading":"API Collection","role":"collectionGroup"},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/loomcore\/transactionsandservices"]}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"sections":[],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/TransactionsAndServices"},"seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/IndexConventions","doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/SafeInterpolation","doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/ConcurrencyModel","doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/StoringCustomTypes","doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/QueryingJSON","doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/FullTextSearch"],"title":"Articles","anchor":"Articles","generated":true}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A transaction wraps a block of operations so they either all succeed and commit, or none of them are visible (rollback). LoomCore exposes this with a single method — the block is async, receives the database it runs on, and may suspend freely:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["let fromID = 1","let toID = 2","let fromBalance = 90.0","let toBalance = 210.0","let journalID = 7","","try await db.transaction { db in","  try await db.exec(\"INSERT INTO accounts (id, balance) VALUES (\\(fromID), \\(fromBalance))\")","  try await db.exec(\"INSERT INTO accounts (id, balance) VALUES (\\(toID), \\(toBalance))\")","  try await db.exec(\"UPDATE journal SET state = \\(\"posted\") WHERE id = \\(journalID)\")","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"If the block returns normally, the transaction commits. If it throws, the transaction rolls back and the error propagates. Atomicity is preserved across ","type":"text"},{"code":"await","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"s inside the block — see the gating section below for how.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Lock modes","anchor":"Lock-modes","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/TransactionKind","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" selects the SQLite locking strategy:"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/TransactionKind\/deferred","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" — default; locks are acquired lazily as needed. Best concurrency, but writes can fail with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SQLITE_BUSY"},{"type":"text","text":" if another connection grabs the write lock first."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/TransactionKind\/immediate","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" — acquires the write lock at "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"BEGIN"},{"type":"text","text":". Use when you know the transaction will write and want to fail fast."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/TransactionKind\/exclusive","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" — acquires an exclusive lock at "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"BEGIN"},{"type":"text","text":". No other connection can read or write. Use sparingly — typically only for migrations."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["try await db.transaction(kind: .immediate) { db in","  \/\/ ...","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"kind"},{"type":"text","text":" applies to the outermost transaction only — nested calls open savepoints, which have no locking mode, so the parameter is ignored for them."}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Nested transactions — savepoints","anchor":"Nested-transactions-savepoints","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Calling "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/Database\/transaction(kind:_:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" from inside an active transaction opens a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SAVEPOINT"},{"type":"text","text":" scope. If the nested block returns normally, the savepoint is released and its work joins the enclosing transaction. If it throws, LoomCore rolls back to the savepoint — undoing only the nested block’s work, leaving the enclosing transaction intact — and rethrows the error:"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["struct NoteRejected: Error {}","","let orderID = 1","let note = \"gift wrap, please\"","","try await db.transaction { db in","  try await db.exec(\"INSERT INTO orders (id) VALUES (\\(orderID))\")","","  do {","    try await db.transaction { db in","      try await db.exec(\"INSERT INTO order_notes (order_id, note) VALUES (\\(orderID), \\(note))\")","      throw NoteRejected()","    }","  } catch is NoteRejected {","    \/\/ The note insert was rolled back; the order insert is still pending.","  }","","  \/\/ Commits the order (without the note).","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Nothing inside a savepoint scope — released or not — becomes durable until the outermost transaction commits. Sibling child tasks that each open a nested transaction are serialized automatically by the gate, so their savepoint scopes never interleave (SQLite savepoints are a stack)."}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Transaction gating","anchor":"Transaction-gating","level":3},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DatabaseActor"},{"type":"text","text":" releases its executor at every suspension point, so an "},{"code":"await","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" inside a transaction body would — without further machinery — let another task’s statements run inside the open transaction. LoomCore prevents this with a gate: while a transaction is in flight, even while its body is suspended, database operations from tasks "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"outside"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" the transaction suspend and resume once the transaction commits or rolls back."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Membership is tracked by a task-local token bound around the block:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Structured children"}]},{"type":"text","text":" ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"async let"},{"type":"text","text":", task groups) and "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"unstructured "},{"code":"Task {}","type":"codeVoice"}]},{"type":"text","text":" inherit the token and operate inside the transaction. An unstructured task must complete before the body returns (await its value); a task that outlives the body races the commit and may run outside the transaction."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"code":"Task.detached","type":"codeVoice"}]},{"type":"text","text":" does not inherit it — a detached task waits at the gate like any outside caller. Awaiting a detached task’s database work from inside the transaction body therefore deadlocks."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An operation waiting at the gate throws "},{"code":"CancellationError","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" if its task is cancelled."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Once past the gate, an operation runs to completion synchronously on "},{"code":"DatabaseActor","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" — interleaving between tasks happens only at gates and suspension points, never mid-statement. When no transaction is active the gate is a single nil check, so ungated workloads pay essentially nothing."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Services-lifecycle-hooks","text":"Services — lifecycle hooks","level":3,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Subclass "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/Database\/Service","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" to react to transaction lifecycle events. Common uses are cache invalidation, change notifications, and audit logging:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["@DatabaseActor","final class Cache {","  private var entries: [String: Int] = [:]","","  func invalidateAll() {","    entries.removeAll()","  }","}","","final class CacheInvalidator: Database.Service {","  let cache = Cache()","","  override func transactionDidCommit() {","    cache.invalidateAll()","  }","}","","let invalidator = await db.getService(CacheInvalidator.self)"]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Services are singletons per ","type":"text"},{"code":"Database","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" instance and per service type. The first ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/Database\/getService(_:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" call constructs the service via the inherited ","type":"text"},{"code":"init(database:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"; subsequent calls return the same instance. Use stored-property defaults (or override ","type":"text"},{"code":"init(database:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" to set them up) for any per-service state.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Services receive ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/Database\/Service\/transactionWillBegin()","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/Database\/Service\/transactionDidCommit()"},{"type":"text","text":", and "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/Database\/Service\/transactionDidRollback()"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"only for the outermost physical transaction"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":". Nested (savepoint) scopes fire no callbacks — they describe intermediate state that only becomes durable when the outer transaction commits. Implicit per-statement transactions (a bare "},{"code":"exec","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" outside a "},{"code":"transaction","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" block) do not fire service callbacks either."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"anchor":"What-rollback-failure-means","type":"heading","text":"What rollback failure means"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Some failures roll the physical transaction back inside SQLite itself — an interrupted write ("},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/Database\/interrupt()"},{"type":"text","text":" or task cancellation) and "},{"code":"ON CONFLICT ROLLBACK","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" constraints both do. LoomCore detects that, skips its own now-pointless "},{"code":"ROLLBACK","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", still notifies services via "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/Database\/Service\/transactionDidRollback()"},{"type":"text","text":", and rethrows the block’s error with the connection intact."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"If "},{"code":"ROLLBACK","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" itself fails on a transaction that is genuinely still open (rare — typically only a corrupt or disconnected database), LoomCore logs a warning, closes the underlying handle, and rethrows the original error from the block. Subsequent operations on the database fail with a closed-database error."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"anchor":"Handling-SQLITEBUSY","type":"heading","text":"Handling SQLITE_BUSY"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A second connection — another process, or another "},{"code":"Database","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" on the same file — can hold a lock that makes a statement fail with "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/SQLiteResultCode\/busy"},{"type":"text","text":". Three tools, in the order to reach for them:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/Database\/setBusyTimeout(milliseconds:)","type":"reference","isActive":true}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" — SQLite retries the lock inside ","type":"text"},{"code":"sqlite3_step","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" for up to the timeout before failing. Keep it modest: the wait sleeps while holding the global ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/DatabaseActor","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":", stalling every ","type":"text"},{"code":"Database","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" in the process for its duration. ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/Database\/interrupt()","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" (and task cancellation) aborts a busy wait.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/TransactionKind\/immediate","type":"reference","isActive":true}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" — a transaction that will write should fail fast at "},{"code":"BEGIN","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" rather than mid-transaction after doing work."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Retry at the call site","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" — for contention that outlasts a reasonable timeout:"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["func withBusyRetry<T>(_ attempts: Int = 3, _ body: () async throws -> T) async throws -> T {","  for _ in 0..<(attempts - 1) {","    do {","      return try await body()","    } catch let error as LoomError where error.sqlite == .busy {","      try await Task.sleep(for: .milliseconds(50))","    }","  }","  return try await body()","}"]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Enabling WAL mode ("},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/Database\/setJournalMode(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":") also removes most reader\/writer contention between connections to the same file."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Atomic operations, savepoint nesting, transaction gating, and lifecycle hooks for cache invalidation."}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore"]]},"kind":"article","topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/Database\/transaction(kind:_:)","doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/TransactionKind","doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/Database\/Service","doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/Database\/getService(_:)","doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/Database\/setBusyTimeout(milliseconds:)","doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/Database\/interrupt()"],"anchor":"Topics"}],"references":{"doc://LoomCore/documentation/LoomCore/TransactionKind/deferred":{"url":"\/documentation\/loomcore\/transactionkind\/deferred","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Defers lock acquisition until the first read or write inside the transaction."}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","title":"TransactionKind.deferred","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"case"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"deferred"}],"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/TransactionKind\/deferred"},"doc://LoomCore/documentation/LoomCore/Database/Service":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/Database\/Service","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Service","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Base class for cross-cutting database services that hook into transaction lifecycle events."}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Service"}],"title":"Database.Service","url":"\/documentation\/loomcore\/database\/service","kind":"symbol"},"doc://LoomCore/documentation/LoomCore/Database/Service/transactionWillBegin()":{"url":"\/documentation\/loomcore\/database\/service\/transactionwillbegin()","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Invoked before each transaction body executes."}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","title":"transactionWillBegin()","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"transactionWillBegin"},{"kind":"text","text":"()"}],"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/Database\/Service\/transactionWillBegin()"},"doc://LoomCore/documentation/LoomCore/TransactionKind/immediate":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/TransactionKind\/immediate","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Acquires a reserved write lock when the transaction begins."}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","title":"TransactionKind.immediate","fragments":[{"text":"case","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"immediate","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/loomcore\/transactionkind\/immediate"},"doc://LoomCore/documentation/LoomCore/Database/transaction(kind:_:)":{"type":"topic","title":"transaction(kind:_:)","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"transaction"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"T"},{"kind":"text","text":">("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"kind"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"TransactionKind","preciseIdentifier":"s:8LoomCore15TransactionKindO"},{"kind":"text","text":", ("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Database","preciseIdentifier":"s:8LoomCore8DatabaseC"},{"kind":"text","text":") "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"async"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"throws"},{"kind":"text","text":" -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"T"},{"kind":"text","text":") "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"async"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"throws"},{"kind":"text","text":" -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"T"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/Database\/transaction(kind:_:)","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Runs a block of operations atomically inside a transaction."}],"url":"\/documentation\/loomcore\/database\/transaction(kind:_:)"},"doc://LoomCore/documentation/LoomCore/SQLiteResultCode/busy":{"type":"topic","title":"busy","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"static"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"busy"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"SQLiteResultCode","preciseIdentifier":"s:8LoomCore16SQLiteResultCodeV"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/SQLiteResultCode\/busy","abstract":[{"text":"Database file could not be written because of concurrent activity by another connection.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/loomcore\/sqliteresultcode\/busy"},"doc://LoomCore/documentation/LoomCore/ConcurrencyModel":{"url":"\/documentation\/loomcore\/concurrencymodel","role":"collectionGroup","title":"Concurrency and Actor Isolation","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/ConcurrencyModel","abstract":[{"text":"How LoomCore makes SQLite race-free without explicit locking.","type":"text"}],"kind":"article"},"doc://LoomCore/documentation/LoomCore/Database/interrupt()":{"url":"\/documentation\/loomcore\/database\/interrupt()","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Interrupts the SQL statement currently executing on this connection."}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","title":"interrupt()","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"interrupt"},{"kind":"text","text":"()"}],"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/Database\/interrupt()"},"doc://LoomCore/documentation/LoomCore/Database/Service/transactionDidCommit()":{"url":"\/documentation\/loomcore\/database\/service\/transactiondidcommit()","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Invoked after a transaction commits successfully."}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","title":"transactionDidCommit()","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"transactionDidCommit"},{"kind":"text","text":"()"}],"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/Database\/Service\/transactionDidCommit()"},"doc://LoomCore/documentation/LoomCore/SafeInterpolation":{"url":"\/documentation\/loomcore\/safeinterpolation","role":"collectionGroup","title":"Safe SQL Interpolation","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/SafeInterpolation","abstract":[{"text":"When ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\\(value)"},{"text":" becomes a parameter, when it becomes literal text, and how to keep injection-prone surfaces small.","type":"text"}],"kind":"article"},"doc://LoomCore/documentation/LoomCore/Database/getService(_:)":{"url":"\/documentation\/loomcore\/database\/getservice(_:)","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Returns the singleton instance of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"type"},{"type":"text","text":" for this database, creating it on first access."}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","title":"getService(_:)","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"getService"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"T"},{"kind":"text","text":">("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"T"},{"kind":"text","text":".Type) -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"T"}],"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/Database\/getService(_:)"},"doc://LoomCore/documentation/LoomCore/FullTextSearch":{"url":"\/documentation\/loomcore\/fulltextsearch","role":"collectionGroup","title":"Full-Text Search","identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/FullTextSearch","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"Match, rank, and excerpt text with typed expressions over SQLite’s FTS5 extension.","type":"text"}],"kind":"article"},"doc://LoomCore/documentation/LoomCore/TransactionKind/exclusive":{"url":"\/documentation\/loomcore\/transactionkind\/exclusive","role":"symbol","title":"TransactionKind.exclusive","identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/TransactionKind\/exclusive","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"Acquires an exclusive lock when the transaction begins.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"text":"case","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"exclusive","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://LoomCore/documentation/LoomCore/QueryingJSON":{"url":"\/documentation\/loomcore\/queryingjson","role":"collectionGroup","title":"Querying JSON","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/QueryingJSON","abstract":[{"text":"Extract, filter, modify, build, and iterate JSON documents with typed expressions over SQLite’s JSON functions.","type":"text"}],"kind":"article"},"doc://LoomCore/documentation/LoomCore/Database/setJournalMode(_:)":{"url":"\/documentation\/loomcore\/database\/setjournalmode(_:)","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/Database\/setJournalMode(_:)","type":"topic","title":"setJournalMode(_:)","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Sets the journal mode and returns the mode actually applied."}],"fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"setJournalMode","kind":"identifier"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"text":"Database","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:8LoomCore8DatabaseC"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"JournalMode","preciseIdentifier":"s:8LoomCore8DatabaseC11JournalModeO"},{"kind":"text","text":") "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"async"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"throws"},{"kind":"text","text":" -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Database","preciseIdentifier":"s:8LoomCore8DatabaseC"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"JournalMode","preciseIdentifier":"s:8LoomCore8DatabaseC11JournalModeO"}],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://LoomCore/documentation/LoomCore/DatabaseActor":{"url":"\/documentation\/loomcore\/databaseactor","role":"symbol","title":"DatabaseActor","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/DatabaseActor","abstract":[{"text":"Global actor that serializes all SQLite access in LoomCore.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"text":"actor","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"DatabaseActor","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"DatabaseActor","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://LoomCore/documentation/LoomCore/StoringCustomTypes":{"url":"\/documentation\/loomcore\/storingcustomtypes","role":"collectionGroup","title":"Storing Custom Types","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/StoringCustomTypes","abstract":[{"text":"How ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Bindable"},{"text":" maps Swift types to SQLite storage, and how to extend it.","type":"text"}],"kind":"article"},"doc://LoomCore/documentation/LoomCore/IndexConventions":{"url":"\/documentation\/loomcore\/indexconventions","role":"collectionGroup","title":"Index Conventions","identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/IndexConventions","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"How LoomCore handles SQLite’s asymmetric 1-based parameter \/ 0-based column indexing.","type":"text"}],"kind":"article"},"doc://LoomCore/documentation/LoomCore/Database/Service/transactionDidRollback()":{"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Invoked after a transaction rolls back, whether explicitly or because the body threw."}],"title":"transactionDidRollback()","identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/Database\/Service\/transactionDidRollback()","url":"\/documentation\/loomcore\/database\/service\/transactiondidrollback()","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"transactionDidRollback"},{"kind":"text","text":"()"}]},"doc://LoomCore/documentation/LoomCore/Database/setBusyTimeout(milliseconds:)":{"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"Sets the busy timeout and returns the value actually applied.","type":"text"}],"title":"setBusyTimeout(milliseconds:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/Database\/setBusyTimeout(milliseconds:)","url":"\/documentation\/loomcore\/database\/setbusytimeout(milliseconds:)","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"setBusyTimeout","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"milliseconds","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:s5Int32V","text":"Int32","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") ","kind":"text"},{"text":"async","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"throws","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" -> ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:s5Int32V","text":"Int32","kind":"typeIdentifier"}]},"doc://LoomCore/documentation/LoomCore/TransactionKind":{"url":"\/documentation\/loomcore\/transactionkind","role":"symbol","title":"TransactionKind","identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/TransactionKind","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"SQLite transaction locking mode.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"TransactionKind","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"TransactionKind","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://LoomCore/documentation/LoomCore":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore","abstract":[{"text":"A type-safe SQLite wrapper for Swift 6+ built on actor isolation.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","title":"LoomCore","role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/loomcore"}}}